.TH TULPAR-VERIFY 1 "2026" "tulpar 0.2.0" "Tulpar Manual"
.SH NAME
tulpar-verify \- verify installed package files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tulpar verify
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B tulpar v
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B tulpar \-v
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Checks that every file recorded for each installed package is still
present on disk, and reports any package with missing files.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dest " " \fIpath\fR
Verify an alternate root instead of the live system.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 if every installed package verified cleanly, non-zero if any file
is missing.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tulpar (1),
.BR tulpar-list (1)
